docs/screenshots/*
# **THE PICTURES ARE GENERATED WHERE THEY ARE SERVED.** `mkdocs build` records
# every narrative through `hooks/pictures.py`, so nothing here needs to be
# committed and nothing here can go stale. The comment this replaced said the
# cost of the old arrangement out loud: the other screenshots "are force-added
# by hand, which means a regenerated one is invisible until somebody
# remembers". A picture nobody regenerates is how a shot of a deleted tab
# survived eight months.
#
# Two exceptions, and both are read where nothing builds them:
#
#   the README's narrative, marked `committed=True` in `dossier.narratives`
#   and recorded by the test suite so a change to it shows up in `git status`;
#
#   the ring's recordings, for the same reason -- the README embeds them.
!docs/screenshots/first-run.gif
!docs/screenshots/rad_ring_*.svg
!docs/screenshots/content_viewer_readme.svg

# Jupyter Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# UV / pip
.uv/
pip-wheel-metadata/
